 r"I am writing to apply for the Data \& Project Analyst position at Lanas Healthcare Technology. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have prepared and checked large datasets, turned them into reports that clients and colleagues act on, and looked for ways to make the process itself faster and more reliable.",

 r"What attracts me most to this role is that the analysis has a visible end point: audit findings and insight reports that help healthcare organisations, including NHS Wales, protect patient information and run services well. The posting describes a role that combines careful data preparation with client delivery and process improvement, and that is the mix of work I enjoy most. I like taking an unclear problem, identifying what the people who own it actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I work with large merchant and transaction datasets in SQL and Python, and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track progress. When I was asked to complete a repetitive configuration task by hand, I worked through a few examples, saw the underlying logic and used Claude Code to build an automated workflow with a validation step to check its own output, which cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent. It taught me that automating a process is only worthwhile if the checks are built in from the start, which is how I would approach reviewing and improving the Python scripts behind Maxwell Stanley's solution.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing healthcare AI project for a pharmaceutical client. I built a regex and LLM extraction pipeline that cleaned and structured more than 4,800 free-text patient consultation threads, designed a 246-question benchmark and rubric with clinical experts that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and presented the findings, risks and recommendations to clinical and business stakeholders. Delivering to a client taught me to agree the quality standard and timeline first, so that the final report answers the question the client actually has.",

